  return manifest_has_world and manifest_has_module and deployed_route_resolves_module;
}

; --- Spec browser witnesses (measured 2026-09-20) -----------------------------------------------
; Read-only GETs. The manifest keys this repository THREE ways and only one of them resembles the
; WORLD string above. The repos entry and the categories key are BARE (turbobaby-user-bot and
; turbobaby-user-bot/specs); the discovery.worlds entry IS owner-qualified, but lower-cased
; (ghashtag/turbobaby-user-bot). Refuted 2026-09-20 by reading discovery.worlds directly: an
; earlier reading of this block said the manifest never keys owner-qualified, and that was wrong.
; What survives is the search warning, and only in its case-sensitive form -- grepping the
; manifest for gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot matches nothing and yields the false reading that this
; world is absent from a manifest that carries it under three keys.
; HTTP status names below. specs/turbobaby/catalog_api.t27 also declares HTTP_OK and
; HTTP_NOT_FOUND, and it owns the outcomes OUR read-only API returns; these are observations of an
; external host, not that contract's vocabulary reused. No REUSES_*_ID is written for it on
; purpose: this file depends on nothing catalog_api decides, and a pointer would invent an edge
; that does not exist.
