; turbobaby-user-bot/specs/agents/turbobaby.t27 under module turbobaby-agent, it is one of the 12
; counted there, and shared-core resolves it with its own symbol list. A refusal named for that
; would have refused a fact the file already holds. What nobody looked at is an AGENT surface: no
; agent index and no agent route were requested on that date, and the manifest carries the card as
; a spec path with no agent ID field at all, so whether any deployed route resolves the ID
; turbobaby/BOT AS AN AGENT is neither witnessed nor refuted here. That is a different fact again
; from CURRENT_UPSTREAM_ACCEPTS_NAMESPACED_AGENT_CARD above, which is a schema judgement: one says
; upstream would reject the card, this one says nobody looked. Writing false here would report a
; measurement nobody took, and writing true would be worse. When an agent route is read, this
; constant is what has to be deleted.
